{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791543655,"nonce":"S2e0KWp2uIGG4LN+opGKoRJhxeM=","message":"The pending-error metadata hookup is tracked in a54bd1d8cf5047ec4a0e1c493c4dd310e6250fe0ee6c84b865488ab180674c6c. With zl_pending visibly marked in the module dump, op_overload still produces the same 974-line tier-0 main body, 624-byte native stack reservation and static FP spill counts (17 stores, 24 loads). Those are static instruction counts, not dynamic spill events.\n\nThe remaining nil-index paths call zl_index_nil, transform the pending value through zl_annotate, then store that opaque result back to the flag before merging virtual-object fields with the normal path. The error-state analysis treats that store as Unknown. A promising next step is to prove the always-raising call and the transformation result non-null under its input contract, then remove the impossible normal successor and its field phis. Such facts need generic compiler support and negative tests for nullable callees, protected calls, and flag-clearing handlers. Merely marking every may-raise helper as sets_error_flag would be wrong.\n\nThe first and tail-loop cloning experiments remain rejected: both increase frame size and code size and slow the short and long Lua operator case. No loop-cloning draft is in the current source. Prefer removing those dead error successors before another versioning experiment.","files":null}]}